=======================================================================================================
FRAME GEOMETRY SURVEY + PROBE CALIBRATION  -  21/08/2026
=======================================================================================================
Session record. Covers Z probe trigger height, the P5/P9 resolution, a bed.g
motor-order bug, and a full gantry geometry survey cross-checked against a
Mitutoyo DTI. Ends with a shim schedule and an order list.

Machine state during all of this: damaged/temporary granite slab fitted, no bed
heater attached, hotend PT1000 still failed (so everything COLD). Replacement
slab on order.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. HEADLINE FINDINGS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*** GEOMETRY IS TEMPERATURE DEPENDENT. Cold numbers are NOT what to build to. ***
Measured cold (~20C frame) and hot (60C chamber / 46C frame, soaked).

a) RIGHT Y RAIL LOW AT REAR - the shimmable fault.
      cold 0.203mm   hot 0.314mm   across the 380mm probe span
   Front rails level in both states (-0.024 cold, -0.019 hot).
   The drop grows progressively rear-ward and grows further with temperature.
   SHIM TO THE HOT FIGURE - section 6.

b) X BEAM INVERTS WITH TEMPERATURE - NOT shimmable. Full numbers in section 5b.
      cold  beam CROWNS UP  0.089mm at mid-span (gantry rides high)
      hot   beam SAGS DOWN  0.186mm at mid-span (gantry rides low)
      swing 0.275mm over dT 26K  =  10.6 microns/K
   Cannot be corrected mechanically. Mesh only.
   DECISION 22/08/2026 (Trev): leave the X beam, shim the Y rail only.
   NOTE this supersedes the earlier "X beam is good, leave it alone" - that
   conclusion was cold-only and is not wrong, just incomplete.

c) Z DATUM SHIFTS 0.877mm between cold and soaked. Whole-loop expansion.
   Harmless IF you re-home and re-tram hot. Fatal if you home cold and print hot.

d) THE ALPS CANNOT COMPLETE A LARGE MESH HOT. It latches "probe already
   triggered" after ~21-25 points (~150-200 strikes) and recovers between runs.
   KNOWN behaviour of this probe on this machine, seen before. Raising the
   deployprobe settle to 800ms and adding M558 R0.4 did NOT help - both reverted.
   USE A COARSE GRID HOT: 4x4 completes reliably, 5x5 is untested and marginal.

e) Both rails bow upward mid-span ~0.2mm, COMMON MODE, no roll induced. Ignore.

f) THE MACHINE IS REPEATABLE. cold run2 vs run3 0.0043mm rms; hot 4x4 A vs B
   0.0064mm rms. The frame is stable at a given temperature.

g) G31 trigger height -0.030 +/-0.005 (slip gauge, tight assembly). Still COLD.
h) M92 Z800 CORRECT, verified by calipers against physical bed travel.

